  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1.1 Number of supported townships which meet set criteria to perform participatory planning effectively (functionality index)
1.2.1 Percentage of grant/project executed within fiscal year
1.2.2 Percentage of projects (a) starting implementation and (b) completed physical and financial progress in line with Grant Manual and Procurement Guidelines

1.2.3 Number of townships where projects meet minimum benchmarks as per Procurement Guidelines
1.3.1 Number of supported townships in which at least five social accountability mechanisms are used
2.1.1 Number of women benefitted (trained) from women empowerment measures enable to advocate for women concerns;
2.2.1 Percentage of W/VTAs that hold and document at least three community consultations on community priorities involving both men and women during the planning process

2.3.1 Percentage of CSO engaged in supported Townships reporting having improved engagement with Township Administrations 
3.1.1 Percentage of grant that funds projects located in EAO areas
3.2.1 Number of supported Townships with EAO areas showing improved engagement between EAOs and TA on service delivery

4.1.1 Number of case studies, policy documents and knowledge products produced based on lesson learned from township planning process, PFM, testing of social accountability, gender actions and engaging CSO in documenting changes at community.
4.1.2 Number of policy dialogues, workshops and learning events that informed policy discussion in relation to scale up and national replication of township planning model</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2017">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1 No structured popular participation and citizen consultation during township planning process
1.2 No grants executed
1.3 No procurement guidelines at township level
1.4 No social accountability mechanisms in place
2.1 No systematic public participation of women in the planning process
2.2 Participatory planning process stipulated in Grant Manual not followed
2.3 No systematic engagement of CSO in planning process
3.1 No project intervention: EAOs not engaged with Township Administrations in planning process
3.2 No project intervention: EAOs not engaged with Township Administrations in planning process
4. No product</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1.2 ;Out of 15 townships at least 12 townships meet level 4 across 4 function
1.2.1; 95% of full grant amount allocated during planning cycle FY 2018/2019 has been liquidated through implementation of planned projects 
1.2.2 ; At least 90% of selected projects from fiscal year 2018-2019 completed physical progress in line with standards as per Grant Manual and Procurement Guidelines 
1.2.3; Out of 15 at least 10 supported townships fully comply with set criteria 
1.3.1: 15 supported townships use at least five and more social accountability mechanisms are used effectively
2.1.1: at least 500 women in all 15 supported townships benefitted from women empowerment measures within the framework of the project 
2.2.1: at least 500 W/VTA in all 15 supported townships hold at least 3 community consultations involving both men and women during the planning process 
2.3.1: 80% of supported CSO in all supported townships reach level 4
3.1.1: No control over the target since the decisions are taken in a consultative and participatory manner at each planning cycle and therefore selected projects will be defined after prioritization with all key stakeholders. 
3.2.1: 75% of supported townships with EAO areas reach Level 4
4.1.1: At least 15 products
4.1.2: 9(cumulative) products</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Updated December 21, 2020
1.1.2; Out of 15 townships 13 meet level 4 across 4 function. Target achieved.
1.2.1; 100% of full grant amount allocated during planning cycle FY 2018/2019 has been liquidated through implementation of planned projects . Target achieved.
1.2.2 ; 100% of selected projects from fiscal year 2018-2019 completed physical progress in line with standards as per Grant Manual and Procurement Guidelines. Target achieved.
1.2.3; Out of 15 townships, 12 fully meet guidelines. Target achieved.
1.3.1: 12 supported townships use at least five social accountability mechanisms. Target achieved.
2.1.1: 580 women across 15 supported townships benefitted from women empowerment measures within the framework of the project . Target partially achieved.
2.2.1: All 15 supported townships held at least 3 community consultations involving both men and women during the planning process. Target achieved. 
2.3.1: 90% of supported CSO reported an improved engagement with Township administrators. Target achieved.
3.1.1: 29.6% of grant allocated to seven TDLG supported townships prioritised for projects in mixed control areas
3.2.1: To be reported in 2020. 
4.1.1: 6 products produced in 2020. Target achieved. 
4.1.2: One event was held to launch the Gender Equality in Public Administration Report. 2 events were postponed, namely the Local Governance Forum and the Technical Working Group. The Local Governance Donor Coordination Group (LGDCG) was used to disseminate accumulated knowledge. Target partially achieved.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
